<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">28 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 28 October, from 312 to 1958.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">312 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,714 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Constantine defeats Maxentius at the Milvian Bridge</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Constantine's army defeated his rival Maxentius outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, and Maxentius drowned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiber-river">Tiber</a>. Constantine credited the Christian God with his victory and went on to legalise and favour <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1492 CE <span class="tih-ago">534 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Columbus reaches Cuba</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On his first voyage, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a> landed on the north-east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>. Convinced he was near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>, he sent envoys inland in search of the court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-khan">Great Khan</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-khan">Great Khan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1886 CE <span class="tih-ago">140 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Statue of Liberty is dedicated in New York Harbor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grover-cleveland">Grover Cleveland</a> dedicated Liberty Enlightening the World, a gift from the people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, on Bedloe's Island. The statue became a symbol of welcome for millions of immigrants.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1940 CE <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Italy invades Greece from Albania</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a>'s forces invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> after Prime Minister Metaxas rejected an ultimatum. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> drove the Italians back into Albania, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> invaded the following spring to rescue its ally.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1958 CE <span class="tih-ago">68 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Angelo Roncalli is elected Pope John XXIII</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The 76-year-old patriarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> was elected pope, widely seen as a caretaker. Within three months he announced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-vatican-council">Second Vatican Council</a>, which transformed the Catholic Church.</p></div></li></ol>
